Subject: [PATCH 16/16] =?UTF-8?q?hw/input:=20gt911=20=E2=80=94=20document?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20the=20level-vs-edge=20INT=20experiment?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tried pure level semantics (pull low and hold until the guest reads):
does NOT fire — the pad is demonstrably LOW at idle (the poll-mode
retry loop's reads do not leave it high as assumed), so there is no
transition to trigger on. Reverted to the working high-then-low assert.
Known cosmetic artifact stays: each press produces a duplicate Begin
under dual-edge irq setups, and the release occasionally drops when
the edge pair races the poll loop — the root cause is where the INT
line idles between polls; next batch instruments gt911_set_int to
settle it.
---
 hw/input/gt911.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/input/gt911.c b/hw/input/gt911.c
index 322909d..14e0690 100644
--- a/hw/input/gt911.c
+++ b/hw/input/gt911.c
@@ -104,7 +104,9 @@ static void gt911_set_int(int level)
 static void gt911_assert_int(void)
 {
     /* high first (the pad can idle low between the poll-mode retries),
-     * then assert — a guaranteed falling edge */
+     * then assert — a guaranteed falling edge. Pure level semantics
+     * (hold low until read) was tried and does NOT fire: the pad is
+     * demonstrably low at idle, leaving no transition to trigger on. */
     gt911_set_int(1);
     gt911_set_int(0);
 }
